I hope someone is cross-checking what I'm saying, because I'm usually
just reading it straight from the source, and it's easy to miss
something when you do that...

> [Thrown Mjollnir has 1/200 chance of hitting you on return, independent
> 20% chance each of targeting wands and rings for destruction, 1/3 chance
> per wand/ring]

> So if you have three wands of death, there's 1 in 1000 chance that 1 of
> them will be destroyed... right? 

19/27000 (~0.07%) that at least one will be destroyed. Independent
probabilities are multiplicative, not additive :-)

> Does MR protect you from being killed this way?

No (if you're at low enough HP for it to), but shock resistance will
protect you against the d10 damage from the exploding wand (as well as
against the damage from Mjollnir hitting you in the first place).
Wands of death don't do any more damage than any other wand blown up
in this fashion.

